# Attributions

This repository is an integration / tuning layer. It builds on the following
open-source projects, whose licenses are respected:

## holographic memory provider
- Project: https://github.com/itpartypattaya/hermes-plugin-holographic
- License: MIT
- Use: the `holographic-semantic` provider in `memory/plugin/` subclasses the
  holographic `HolographicMemoryProvider` at load time. The original plugin is
  NOT modified or vendored here; install it separately. The fact-store schema
  (`facts(fact_id, content, tags, trust_score)`) and the lexical retriever come
  from holographic.

## bge-m3 embedding model
- Project: https://github.com/FlagOpen/FlagEmbedding (BAAI/bge-m3)
- Model:   https://huggingface.co/BAAI/bge-m3
- License: MIT
- Use: the local embedding sidecar in `memory/sidecar/` loads bge-m3 weights to
  produce normalized sentence embeddings. Model weights are NOT redistributed
  here; download them yourself (see memory/sidecar/README.md).

## Hermes Agent
- Project: https://github.com/NousResearch/hermes-agent
- License: MIT, Copyright (c) 2025 Nous Research
- Use: the host agent framework. The memory provider plugin API
  (`plugins.memory.import_provider_module`), the Desktop settings contract, and the
  skills format come from Hermes Agent.
- `patches/hermes-agent-*.patch` are modifications of the Hermes Agent source at the
  fixed commits listed in `patches/README.md`, distributed under the same MIT license
  with the original copyright notice. They are not an official Hermes release.

The eval methodology, the hybrid fusion logic, the Chinese-oriented tuning, and
the sidecar serving/caching/fallback code are original work in this repository,
released under the MIT License (see LICENSE).